<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamad bin Abdullah Al Sharqi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamad bin Abdullah Al Sharqi was the chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharqiyin">Sharqiyin</a> tribe of Fujairah on the east coast of the Arabian peninsula. In 1902 he asserted Fujairah's independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Qawasim</a> of Sharjah, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> continued to regard it as part of Sharjah. His family has ruled Fujairah since, and Britain recognised it as a separate trucial state in 1952.</p></div>
